// php/php-02: the files PHPStan analyses.
//
// PHPStan parses a file before any rule sees it, and a file its parser rejects gets only the parse error
// (phpstan.parse, FileAnalyser's ParserErrorsException): no rule runs on any of its lines. A syntax error here is
// what tree-sitter-php finds, an ERROR node, as the product's own path skips such a file ("file has syntax errors").
//   function f() {}  class True {}      no missingType.return at f: the file does not parse
// Psalm is not so: it reports ParseError and analyses the statements its parser recovers.
//
// What a rule gets from this library:
//   php_parse_error(d)   document d has a syntax error
//
// Builds on core only.

.decl php_parse_error(d: number)
php_parse_error(d) :- kind(e, "ERROR"), docof(e, d).
